 "title": "Register of Deeds - Edmunds County, South Dakota",
 "text": "Register of Deeds - Edmunds County, South Dakota\nOctober 18, 2026\nEdmunds County, South Dakota\nHome\nAbout\nHistory\nDirectory »\nAuditor\nClerk of Courts\nHighway Department\nEmergency Management\nDirector of Equalization\n4-H Program\nPlanning & Zoning\nPublic Health\nRegister of Deeds\nTreasurer\nSheriff\nStates Attorney\nWelfare\nVeteran Services\nCommission »\nCommission Agenda\nCommission Minutes\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Ordinances\nCounty Financials\nForms\nNotices\nEmployment\nQuick Links\nRegister of Deeds\nGwen Geditz\n210 2nd Ave Ste 205\nPO Box 386\nIpswich, SD 57451\nPhone: 605-426-6431\nFax: 605-426-6164\nEmail: gwen.geditz@midco.net\nThe county Register of Deeds issues and files marriage licenses, birth and death certificates, burial permits, real estate transactions (including deeds, mortgages and mortgage transfers), federal and state tax liens, state unemployment tax, military discharge records, businesses and new business. The Register of Deeds is also responsible for recording all liens, cancel liens, survey plat certificates and county welfare liens. The Register of Deeds is the official county record keeper .\nApplication for a Birth Record\nApplication for a Marriage Record\nApplication for a Death Record\nCounty Procedures For E-recording\nWebsite to access Birth Records 100 years and older: http://apps.sd.gov/PH14Over100BirthRec/index.aspx\nCommissioner Meeting October 27, 2026 9:00 am – 12:00 pm\nCommissioner Meeting November 5, 2026 9:00 am – 12:00 pm\nCommissioner Meeting November 24, 2026 9:00 am – 12:00 pm\nClosed – Thanksgiving November 26, 2026 All-day\nClosed – Thanksgiving November 27, 2026 All-day\nNEW Edmunds County GIS Website!\nhttps://www.1stdistrict.org/edmundsts/\nReturn to top of page\nCopyright © 2026 on Genesis Framework · WordPress · Log in",
